{"parentUuid":"bb3b146d-a498-44f5-a026-1e62f08b505a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgaiEFoqwid7vxcdeeMwx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The A7 live exit is underway, but not finished. The build turn for job `j7eb804a7` (from issue #1, \"Add a power(a, b) function\", in `ianparo/bastion`) has run for more than 10 minutes and is still going.\n\n**Done so far:**\n- **Repo:** it's private and set as the `bastion-gh` workspace. I added that workspace with a direct database write rather than through the Settings form.\n- **Forge:** set to GitHub, saved as settings version 1, \"forge: local -> github\".\n- **Issue to job:** issue #1 started the job from New request, and the job page links back to it.\n- **Plan:** written and approved.\n\n**The build is slow:** the plan proposed moving the tests into a new `tests/` folder, and the agent is now shuffling test files around. The repo's hook refused one `rm` (audit entry #537), and the agent kept going with `git mv` and commits. When it reaches review, the `tests-kept` check will flag any deleted test in the diff.\n\n**Webview crash:** the app's page went blank, and its WebKit content process was gone. I relaunched the app; the job lives in the store, so nothing was lost. I don't know the cause; it happened right after a scroll on the job page.\n\n**Waiting:** a background task will report when the build ends, with a fallback check in about 25 minutes. Then I'll approve at review, which pushes the branch and opens the pull request on GitHub. CI should fail on the missing `CHANGELOG.md` entry, and the agent's fix turn should correct it. Once CI passes, I'll stop for you to approve the merge, then do the settings restore check."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":255,"cache_read_input_tokens":857700,"output_tokens":532,"output_tokens_details":{"th