{"parentUuid":"914d834e-4905-4a77-abf0-0a09a63e2374","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgaiZncXcqnxJ2KAw3MMz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Job `j7eb804a7` is back in build with my note. The first build left the repo's tests in two places, so pytest failed. My note told the agent to reset to `origin/main` and add `power(a, b)` plus one test to the existing `test_calc.py`. A background task will report when it reaches review.\n\n**The freeze is probably not Bastion's.** It came back even with spellcheck off, with the same stack. Something asked the webview for `AXVisibleCharacterRange`, and WebKit walked the whole page to answer. My test driver (cmux-cua) reads that attribute after every scroll and typed text, so it's the likely trigger, not macOS text checking. Driving with plain keys (End, Page Up) instead of wheel scrolls, the note typed in without a freeze. Spellcheck-off stays, since it's harmless; it just wasn't the fix. I haven't confirmed whether a screen reader like VoiceOver would set off the same freeze. I'll correct the plan's note on this.\n\n**Next:** approve at review, which pushes the branch and opens the pull request. CI should fail on the missing `CHANGELOG.md` entry, and the agent's fix turn should correct it. Once CI passes, the job waits for your merge decision; then I'll run the settings restore check."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":506,"cache_read_input_tokens":898081,"output_tokens":419,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":506,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":419,"cache_read_input_tokens":898081,"cache_creation_input_tokens":506,"cache_creation"