{"parentUuid":"a401785a-aca1-43db-a6d6-e237e76097dd","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"1f2047be-0068-46f0-a2a5-bab29cbcd70a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GW9fSKifyo6ih7Wk5vcyR2","type":"tool_result","content":"fn commented(job: &mut Job, text: &str, dials: &Dials) -> Vec<Effect> {\n    if let Some(question) = job.question.take() {\n        job.feedback = Some(format!(\"You asked: {question}\\nThe answer: {text}\"));\n    } else {\n        job.feedback = Some(text.into());\n        job.stage = match job.stage {\n            Stage::Approve => Stage::Plan,\n            Stage::Review => Stage::Build,\n            other => other,\n        };\n        job.failures = 0;\n    }\n    enter(job, dials)\n}\nYou asked: The owner instructed to reset with `git -C /work/repo reset --hard origin/main` but origin/main isn't available in this environment (git error: unknown revision). I can proceed two ways — either (A) remove the duplicate top-level test file test_calc.py (so only tests/test_calc.py remains) and commit, or (B) keep the top-level test (as owner later requested) and instead remove or rename tests/test_calc.py to avoid the pytest name clash. However the job constraints include \"Do not delete existing tests.\" I need explicit guidance: which test file should remain (top-level test_calc.py or tests/test_calc.py), and do you permit renaming one of them rather than deleting?\nThe answer: Undo every commit since the start instead: run git -C /work/repo reset --hard @{u} (the branch you started from). That restores the original state with only the top-level test_calc.py and no tests/ folder, and deletes no test of the original repo. Then add power(a, b) to calc.py and one test_power test to the top-level test_calc.py, and commit.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"c2d8136a-081a-475d-b942-d9675d38be2d","timestamp":"2026-10-31T17:35:54.772Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"fn commented(job: &mut Job, text: &str, dials: &Dials) -> Vec<Effect> {\n    if let Some(question) = job.question.take() {\n        job.feedback = Some(format!(\"You asked: {question}\\nThe answer: {text}\"));\n    } else {\n        job.feedback = Some(text.into());\n        job.stage = match job.stage {\n            Stage::Approve => Stage::Plan,\n            Stage::Review => Stage::Build,\n            other => other,\n        };\n        job.failures = 0;\n    }\n    enter(job, dials)\n}\nYou asked: The owner instructed to reset with `git -C /work/repo reset --hard origin/main` but origin/main isn't available in this environment (git error: unknown revision). I can proceed two ways — either (A) remove the duplicate top-level test file test_calc.py (so only tests/test_calc.py remains) and commit, or (B) keep the top-level test (as owner later requested) and instead remove or rename tests/test_calc.py to avoid the pytest name clash. However the job constraints include \"Do not delete existing tests.\" I need explicit guidance: which test file should remain (top-level test_calc.py or tests/test_calc.py), and do you permit renaming one of them rather than deleting?\nThe answer: Undo every commit since the start instead: run git -C /work/repo reset --hard @{u} (the branch you started from). That restores the original state with only the top-level test_calc.py and no tests/ folder, and deletes no test of the original repo. Then add power(a, b) to calc.py and one test_power test to the top-level test_calc.py, and commit.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"5844b2d9-8f5a-48dd-ae5d-74d691d99711","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","root":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","branch":"main","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":null,"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[],"visibility_cache":[]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/tac