{"parentUuid":"27ee8151-a5f7-4de0-aac2-a251394aa229","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgajCtiAkQ5fpUzu4N9W6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Clippy came back clean, and the Approve label on the Jobs list is just a badge, not a button, which I'd clicked by mistake earlier. I'm logging the A7 exit in the plan, but A7 stays open until you merge PR #2.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":953,"cache_read_input_tokens":901422,"output_tokens":1534,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":105},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":953,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1534,"cache_read_input_tokens":901422,"cache_creation_input_tokens":953,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":953},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"fe4ad8ff-9047-4df0-9424-74f185d8b7e1","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgajCtKrzDs62XXbksnSi","type":"assistant","uuid":"149753c8-b546-4864-a5d7-a32e2dc9303d","timestamp":"2026-10-31T17:42:59.859Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"135a2369-1f42-433b-aacc-5c1b0ce18b48","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"135a2369-1f42-433b-aacc-5c1b0ce18b48","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"pure-pondering-goose"}
{"parentUuid":"149753c8-b546-4864-a5d7-a32e2dc9303d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgajCtiAkQ5fpUzu4N9W6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DY3zZir7tqLiF8xUNh1Zos","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cargo +1.97.0 test --workspace 2>&1 | grep -E \"test result: ok. [1-9]|FAILED|panicked\" && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='PLAN.md'; s=open(p).read()\na=\"| A7 to A13 | — | — |\"\nb=\"\"\"| A7 | in progress | Built (3605253): the GitHub forge (push `bastion/<job>`, open or reuse the pull request, poll its checks, a bounded CI fix turn with the failing log, merge on Approve), issues as requests that link back and close on merge, versioned settings with Restore, oversight presets, a model per stage from `llm-router`, and the Accounts list; the governance pages split into Constraints, Capabilities and Audit Log with Lucide icons (dbe1cf7). 57 core tests, 66 app tests. Live exit (2026-10-31) on `ianparo/bastion` (private, CI runs pytest and needs a CHANGELOG.md entry): job `j7eb804a7` started from issue #1 and links to it; it opened pull request #2 (`bastion/j7eb804a7`, body `Closes #1`); CI failed on the changelog, Bastion sent the fix turn with the CI log (ci_fixes 1), the fixed change was pushed to the same pull request, and CI passed. Settings: forge set to GitHub (v1), the medium preset set both dials to hold (v2), Restore of v1 wrote v3 with the dials back at ask, and the next job (`ja0b04eb6`) waited at approve with no hold timer. Left for the owner: the merge of pull request #2. |\n| A8 to A13 | — | — |\"\"\"\nassert s.count(a)==1; s=s.replace(a,b)\ns=s.rstrip(\"\\n\")+\"\"\"\n\n**What A7 found:**\n\n- The fix turn after CI's first failure changed nothing that fixed it: the\n  log it got was `gh run view --log-failed` cut to its last 4000 characters,\n  and the failing message sat in the middle of the step's environment dump.\n  It took a note from the owner to add the CHANGELOG line. A fix turn needs\n  the failing step's own error lines, not the tail of the log.\n- The agent asks before acting on an owner's note, and once ignored part of\n  one (it moved the tests into `tests/` after being told to keep them at the\n  root). `origin/main` does not exist in the VM: the branch it starts from is\n  `@{u}`.\n- The webview freeze in A5 came back with spellcheck off. A sample showed the\n  same `AXVisibleCharacterRange` walk; the trigger is the test driver, which\n  reads that attribute after scrolls and typing, not macOS text checking.\n  Driving with keys (Page Down, End) avoided it. Whether VoiceOver does the\n  same has not been checked.\n- A settings change pushed nothing, so the other sections of the page kept\n  the old values; each settings command now pushes a change.\n- The `Approve` and `Review` labels on the Jobs list are badges, not buttons,\n  and read as buttons.\n\"\"\"\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngit add -A && git commit -q -m \"A7 live exit: settings changes push, and the plan records the exit\n\nEach settings command now pushes a change, so every section of the\nSettings page reads the new version; live, Checkpoints and History kept\nthe old values after a preset. PLAN.md records the A7 live exit on\nianparo/bastion and what it found.\" && git log --oneline -1","description":"Test, record the exit, commit","timeout":600000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":953,"cache_read_input_tokens":901422,"output_tokens":1534,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":105},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":953,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1534,"cache_read_input_tokens":901422,"cache_creation_input_tokens":953,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_in