{"parentUuid":"aac4f4e9-9649-4e4c-93a4-a376af87c478","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgajUr1A84DRivGFdgXLJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"My earlier finding was off: the agent got the log showing the missing CHANGELOG entry and still skipped it. I'm correcting the plan note, then trimming the log's noise so the error is easier to see.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1917,"cache_read_input_tokens":914625,"output_tokens":1986,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":284},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1917,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1986,"cache_read_input_tokens":914625,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1917,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1917},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"10cd4bb8-1a92-46ce-a4d0-b2f4caa5eb58","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgajUqMhtEVuDjGpdcx6W","type":"assistant","uuid":"dfe9f503-ac4f-4d88-b05a-64df99efa556","timestamp":"2026-10-31T17:46:38.208Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"135a2369-1f42-433b-aacc-5c1b0ce18b48","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"135a2369-1f42-433b-aacc-5c1b0ce18b48","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"pure-pondering-goose"}
{"parentUuid":"dfe9f503-ac4f-4d88-b05a-64df99efa556","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgajUr1A84DRivGFdgXLJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QPbsZR56my7bT3PrqBiHmG","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"rm crates/bastion-spikes/examples/first_message.rs && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='src-tauri/src/forge.rs'; s=open(p).read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(a)==1,a; s=s.replace(a,b)\nrep(\"\"\"        Ok(Checks::Failed(tail(&log)))\"\"\",\"\"\"        Ok(Checks::Failed(tail(&clean(&log))))\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"/// The end of a log, as much as a fix turn reads.\"\"\",\"\"\"/// A `gh run view --log-failed` log as a fix turn should read it: each\n/// line without its job, step and timestamp columns, and without the setup\n/// lines GitHub folds into groups (the command and its environment).\nfn clean(log: &str) -> String {\n    let mut folded = false;\n    let mut out = Vec::new();\n    for line in log.lines() {\n        let text = line.splitn(3, '\\\\t').nth(2).unwrap_or(line);\n        let text = text.trim_start_matches('\\\\u{feff}');\n        let text = match text.split_once(' ') {\n            Some((stamp, rest)) if stamp.len() > 20 && stamp.ends_with('Z') => rest,\n            _ => text,\n        };\n        if text.starts_with(\"##[group]\") {\n            folded = true;\n        } else if text.starts_with(\"##[endgroup]\") {\n            folded = false;\n        } else if !folded {\n            out.push(text.trim_start_matches(\"##[error]\"));\n        }\n    }\n    out.join(\"\\\\n\")\n}\n\n/// The end of a log, as much as a fix turn reads.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"    #[test]\n    fn a_long_log_keeps_its_end() {\"\"\",\"\"\"    #[test]\n    fn a_log_keeps_its_errors_and_drops_its_columns_and_setup() {\n        let log = \"test\\\\tChangelog\\\\t\\\\u{feff}2026-10-31T17:37:30.6227850Z ##[group]Run python check.py\\\\n\\\\\n                   test\\\\tChangelog\\\\t2026-10-31T17:37:30.6255863Z   pythonLocation: /opt/x\\\\n\\\\\n                   test\\\\tChangelog\\\\t2026-10-31T17:37:30.6257695Z ##[endgroup]\\\\n\\\\\n                   test\\\\tChangelog\\\\t2026-10-31T17:37:30.6505436Z CHANGELOG.md has no entry for this change.\\\\n\\\\\n                   test\\\\tChangelog\\\\t2026-10-31T17:37:30.6547741Z ##[error]Process completed with exit code 1.\";\n        assert_eq!(clean(log), \"CHANGELOG.md has no entry for this change.\\\\nProcess completed with exit code 1.\");\n    }\n\n    #[test]\n    fn a_long_log_keeps_its_end() {\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\n\np='PLAN.md'; s=open(p).read()\na=\"\"\"- The fix turn after CI's first failure changed nothing that fixed it: the\n  log it got was `gh run view --log-failed` cut to its last 4000 characters,\n  and the failing message sat in the middle of the step's environment dump.\n  It took a note from the owner to add the CHANGELOG line. A fix turn needs\n  the failing step's own error lines, not the tail of the log.\"\"\"\nb=\"\"\"- The fix turn after CI's first failure changed nothing that fixed it, though\n  its brief held the whole failing log, \"CHANGELOG.md has no entry\" included,\n  between a step's environment dump and its timestamps. It took a note from\n  the owner to add the line. The log is now cleaned to the failing lines\n  before it goes into the brief; whether gpt-5-mini then acts on it is not\n  yet measured.\n- Approve at land merged pull request #2 (2beb204), the branch was deleted,\n  issue #1 closed, and the workspace's `main` pulled the merge.\"\"\"\nassert s.count(a)==1; s=s.replace(a,b)\ns=s.replace(\"| A7 | in progress |\",\"| A7 | done |\",1)\ns=s.replace(\"Left for the owner: the merge of pull request #2. |\",\"Approve at land then merged pull request #2 into `main` (2beb204) and issue #1 closed. Not run live: a fix turn that fixes CI by itself (see below). |\",1)\ns=s.replace(\"| A8 to A13 | — | — |\",\"| A8 | next | — |\\n| A9 to A13 | — | — |\",1)\nopen(p,'w').