N9: `judge::evaluate` has no provider worker in this stack, so a run is graded by a harness turn with no tools; `harness::metrics` meters each session (docs/levels.md). Build (38519c5): `Dials::trial` in the core (a trial approves its own plan and stops at review with its diff, so nothing lands), the core's `eval` module (arms, tally from the audit, totals, differences, grade), an arm's rungs applied per trial job in the gate, every turn of every job metered into `turns`, the eval tables, and the Evals page. 51 core tests, 58 app tests. Live exit (2026-10-31), eval `ee8eaaddd` on `demo-a` from `d6227b2`: three requests that each ask for a `wc` count, A with `no-wc` told and B with it enforced. All six runs reached review and were graded. In total B differs from A: refused 0 -> 5, review findings 2 -> 0, turns 39 -> 28, calls 33 -> 17, cost $0.0344 -> $0.0207; grades 7 and 7. Each request lists B's refused calls with their audit entries (#375, #405, #363, #452, ...) and links to the trial job, which shows it stopped at review with Land pending. Apply B set `no-wc` to enforced and the audit recorded `ee8eaaddd arm b: Told -> Enforced` (#487) and the eval the owner acted on (#488). Not varied yet: the model per stage and the pipeline, since there is one of each until A7 and A8. |","-| A7 | in progress | Built (3605253): the GitHub forge (push `bastion/<job>`, open or reuse the pull request, poll its checks, a bounded CI fix turn with the failing log, merge on Approve), issues as requests that link back and close on merge, versioned settings with Restore, oversight presets, a model per stage from `llm-router`, and the Accounts list; the governance pages split into Constraints, Capabilities and Audit Log with Lucide icons (dbe1cf7). 57 core tests, 66 app tests. Live exit (2026-10-31) on `ianparo/bastion` (private, CI runs pytest and needs a CHANGELOG.md entry): job `j7eb804a7` started from issue #1 and links to it; it opened pull request #2 (`bastion/j7eb804a7`, body `Closes #1`); CI failed on the changelog, Bastion sent the fix turn with the CI log (ci_fixes 1), the fixed change was pushed to the same pull request, and CI passed. Settings: forge set to GitHub (v1), the medium preset set both dials to hold (v2), Restore of v1 wrote v3 with the dials back at ask, and the next job (`ja0b04eb6`) waited at approve with no hold timer. Left for the owner: the merge of pull request #2. |","-| A8 to A13 | — | — |","+| A7 | done | Built (3605253): the GitHub forge (push `bastion/<job>`, open or reuse the pull request, poll its checks, a bounded CI fix turn with the failing log, merge on Approve), issues as requests that link back and close on merge, versioned settings with Restore, oversight presets, a model per stage from `llm-router`, and the Accounts list; the governance pages split into Constraints, Capabilities and Audit Log with Lucide icons (dbe1cf7). 57 core tests, 66 app tests. Live exit (2026-10-31) on `ianparo/bastion` (private, CI runs pytest and needs a CHANGELOG.md entry): job `j7eb804a7` started from issue #1 and links to it; it opened pull request #2 (`bastion/j7eb804a7`, body `Closes #1`); CI failed on the changelog, Bastion sent the fix turn with the CI log (ci_fixes 1), the fixed change was pushed to the same pull request, and CI passed. Settings: forge set to GitHub (v1), the medium preset set both dials to hold (v2), Restore of v1 wrote v3 with the dials back at ask, and the next job (`ja0b04eb6`) waited at approve with no hold timer. Approve at land then merged pull request #2 into `main` (2beb204) and issue #1 closed. Not run live: a fix turn that fixes CI by itself (see below). |","+| A8 | next | — |","+| A9 to A13 | — | — |"," | Later (§10) | on hold | — |"," "," **What A1 found:**"]},{"oldStart":788,"oldLines":11,"newStart":789,"newLines":14,"lines":[" "," **What A7 found:**"," ","-- The fix turn after CI's first failure changed nothing that fixed it: the","-  log it got was `gh run view --log-failed` cut to its last 4000 characters,","-  and the failing message sat in the middle of the step's environment dump.","-  It took a note from the owner to add the CHANGELOG line. A fix turn needs","-  the failing step's own error lines, not the tail of the log.","+- The fix turn after CI's first failure changed nothing that fixed it, though","+  its brief held the whole failing log, \"CHANGELOG.md has no entry\" included,","+  between a step's environment dump and its timestamps. It took a note from","+  the owner to add the line. The log is now cleaned to the failing lines","+  before it goes into the brief; whether gpt-5-mini then acts on it is not","+  yet measured.","+- Approve at land merged pull request #2 (2beb204), the branch was deleted,","+  issue #1 closed, and the workspace's `main` pulled the merge."," - The agent asks before acting on an owner's note, and once ignored part of","   one (it moved the tests into `tests/` after being told to keep them at the","   root). `origin/main` does not exist in the VM: the branch it starts from is"]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/crates/bastion-spikes/examples/first_message.rs","hunks":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":13,"newStart":0,"newLines":0,"lines":["-//! Print a session's first user message: `cargo run -p bastion-spikes --example first_message -- <session>`.","-use bastion_spikes::{call, connect};","-use serde_json::json;","-#[tokio::main]","-async fn main() {","-    let s = std::env::args().nth(1).expect(\"session\");","-    let iii = connect(\"spike-first\");","-    let out = call(&iii, \"session::messages\", json!({ \"session_id\": s })).await.expect(\"messages\");","-    let first = out[\"messages\"].as_array().into_iter().flatten().find(|m| m[\"message\"][\"role\"] == \"user\");","-    let text: Vec<&str> = first.map(|m| m[\"message\"][\"content\"].as_array().into_iter().flatten().filter_map(|p| p[\"text\"].as_str()).collect()).unwrap_or_default();","-    println!(\"{}\", text.join(\"\\n\"));","-    std::process::exit(0);","-}"]}],"deleted":true},{"filePath":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/src-tauri/src/forge.rs","hunks":[{"oldStart":140,"oldLines":7,"newStart":140,"newLines":7,"lines":["                     .unwrap_or_else(|e| e),","             );","         }","-        Ok(Checks::Failed(tail(&log)))","+        Ok(Checks::Failed(tail(&clean(&log))))","     }"," ","     pub async fn merge(&self, pr: &str) -> Result<(), String> {"]},{"oldStart":182,"oldLines":6,"newStart":182,"newLines":30,"lines":["     }"," }"," ","+/// A `gh run view --log-failed` log as a fix turn should read it: each","+/// line without its job, step and timestamp columns, and without the setup","+/// lines GitHub folds into groups (the command and its environment).","+fn clean(log: &str) -> String {","+    let mut folded = false;","+    let mut out = Vec::new();","+    for line in log.lines() {","+        let text = line.splitn(3, '\\t').nth(2).unwrap_or(line);","+        let text = text.trim_start_matches('\\u{feff}');","+        let text = match text.split_once(' ') {","+            Some((stamp, rest)) if stamp.len() > 20 && stamp.ends_with('Z') => rest,","+            _ => text,","+        };","+        if text.starts_with(\"##[group]\") {","+            folded = true;","+        } else if text.starts_with(\"##[endgroup]\") {","+            folded = false;","+        } else if !folded {","+            out.push(text.trim_start_matches(\"##[error]\"));","+        }","+    }","+    out.join(\"\\n\")","+}","+"," /// The end of a log, as much as a fix turn reads."," fn tail(log: &str) -> String {","     if log.is_empty() {"]},{"oldStart":316,"oldLines":6,"newStart":340,"newLines":19,"lines":["         assert!(!describe(&job, \"main\", None).body.contains(\"Closes\"));","     }"," ","+    #[test]","+    fn a_log_keeps_its_errors_and_drops_its_columns_and_setup() {","+        let log = \"test\\tChangelog\\t\\u{feff}2026-10-31T17:37:30.6227850Z ##[group]Run python check.py\\n\\","+                   test\\tChangelog\\t2026-10-31T17:37:30.6255863Z   pythonLocation: /opt/x\\n\\","+                   test\\tChangelog\\t2026-10-31T17:37:30.6257695Z ##[endgroup]\\n\\","+                   test\\tChangelog\\t2026-10-31T17:37:30.6505436Z CHANGELOG.md has no entry for this change.\\n\\","+                   test\\tChangelog\\t2026-10-31T17:37:30.6547741Z ##[error]Process completed with exit code 1.\";","+        assert_eq!(","+            clean(log),","+            \"CHANGELOG.md has no entry for this change.\\nProcess completed with exit code 1.\"","+        );","+    }","+","     #[test]","     fn a_long_log_keeps_its_end() {","         let log = \"x\".repeat(LOG_CHARS) + \"the failure\";"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/PLAN.md","/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/crates/bastion-spikes/examples/first_message.rs","/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/src-tauri/src/forge.rs"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"10cd4bb8-1a92-46ce-a4d0-b2f4caa5eb58","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","root":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","branch":"main","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":1},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":null,"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[],"visibility_cache":[]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a53acc68-2512-4509-bb7d-5855a821a4d5","session_id":"135a2369-1f42-433b-aacc-5c1b0ce18b48","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"135a2369-1f42-433b-aacc-5c1b0ce18b48","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"pure-pondering-goose"}
