{"parentUuid":"06ed3f6e-407b-434b-86d0-5fb9d39f113f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgajytrMZaof65dpaC8tQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XTYxrL2vuHPCPoMGfGCcWy","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='PLAN.md'; s=open(p).read()\na=\"| D23 |\"\ni=s.index(a); j=s.index(\"\\n\",i)\nrow=\"\"\"\n| D25 | Every constraint and capability belongs to one layer. The charter is the repository's own, read from it (`.claude/settings.json` today). The harness runs an agent's turn and binds its calls. The factory moves a job through its pipeline and binds review, land, pull requests and merges. The Constraints and Capabilities pages each show the three. | The owner's words: a charter belongs to a repo, and the harness and factory are Bastion's, built on iii. A rule is easier to judge when its place is plain. |\n| D26 | The harness and the factory change by changing the iii stack, with no code change: their rules, grants and defaults are data the stack carries, not constants in Bastion's code. | The owner's choice. Today the owner's default constraints and grants are seeded from `bastion_core::govern`; moving them into the stack's configuration is the next step (A8). |\"\"\"\ns=s[:j]+row+s[j:]\ns=s.replace(\"| A8 | next | — |\",\"| A8 | next | First: D26, the harness and factory defaults out of code and into the stack's configuration; the governance pages now show charter, harness and factory sections (D25). |\",1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ncargo +1.97.0 fmt --all -- --check && scripts/check-seams.sh && cargo +1.97.0 clippy --workspace --exclude bastion-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings 2>&1 | grep -E \"^(error|warning)\" -A6 | head; cargo +1.97.0 test --workspace 2>&1 | grep -E \"test result: ok. [1-9]|FAILED|panicked\"","description":"Record D25 and D26, run all checks","timeout":600000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null