{"parentUuid":"1055538d-2c6b-4cae-a442-e18904bfe5ff","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"308e8c31-5fd4-40b1-81e6-44b965f525e2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XTYxrL2vuHPCPoMGfGCcWy","type":"tool_result","content":"seams ok\nerror[E0063]: missing field `allow` in initializer of `charter::Charter`\n   --> src-tauri/src/gate.rs:813:9\n    |\n813 |         Charter {\n    |         ^^^^^^^ missing `allow`\n\nFor more information about this error, try `rustc --explain E0063`.\nerror: could not compile `bastion` (lib test) due to 1 previous error\nwarning: build failed, waiting for other jobs to finish...","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"4fada2d4-3be6-4a1a-b8b4-e9fb1d9ca386","timestamp":"2026-10-31T17:53:26.884Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"seams ok\nerror[E0063]: missing field `allow` in initializer of `charter::Charter`\n   --> src-tauri/src/gate.rs:813:9\n    |\n813 |         Charter {\n    |         ^^^^^^^ missing `allow`\n\nFor more information about this error, try `rustc --explain E0063`.\nerror: could not compile `bastion` (lib test) due to 1 previous error\nwarning: build failed, waiting for other jobs to finish...","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"returnCodeInterpretation":"No matches found","noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/PLAN.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":116,"oldLines":6,"newStart":116,"newLines":8,"lines":[" | D21 | The audit record is a hash chain with one writer. Each entry carries an HMAC-SHA256 of its fields and the entry before it, keyed with a secret kept in the macOS Keychain, not in the record, and verification walks the chain. | Any change to a past entry breaks the chain, and whoever can edit the database cannot recompute it without the Keychain key. It still cannot stop a change, or detect entries cut from the end; a remote append-only copy (§10) closes that, later. |"," | D22 | An eval compares two harness configurations on the same requests and the same workspace snapshots, and reports the difference with the hook decisions behind it. | A promotion or demotion comes with evidence, not a guess. |"," | D23 | Forge, tracker, CI, model providers and notifications are adapters behind seams, chosen in Settings. A new product is a new adapter, not a core change. | The owner keeps the tools they already use. |","+| D25 | Every constraint and capability belongs to one layer. The charter is the repository's own, read from it (`.claude/settings.json` today). The harness runs an agent's turn and binds its calls. The factory moves a job through its pipeline and binds review, land, pull requests and merges. The Constraints and Capabilities pages each show the three. | The owner's words: a charter belongs to a repo, and the harness and factory are Bastion's, built on iii. A rule is easier to judge when its place is plain. |","+| D26 | The harness and the factory change by changing the iii stack, with no code change: their rules, grants and defaults are data the stack carries, not constants in Bastion's code. | The owner's choice. Today the owner's default constraints and grants are seeded from `bastion_core::govern`; moving them into the stack's configuration is the next step (A8). |"," "," ## 4. The repository"," "]},{"oldStart":651,"oldLines":7,"newStart":653,"newLines":7,"lines":[" | A5 | done | The gate, the ladders and the audit chain in `bastion-core` (def679b); the governance tables, the hook and the owner's commands (a509bb1); held calls and the Governance page (b4f2704). First live exit on `j4825765c` (ee4435e): a plan's write held, Allow once ran exactly it, Refuse reached the agent, `keep-tests` passed a `git rm` at checked and refused it at enforced, and verification failed after one byte of entry 20 changed. Then, from what that exit found: the review page freeze (513da6c); a keyed chain, its writer's state with a 5 s limit per write, and export (d0d3a27); charter constraints and repository hooks from `.claude/settings.json` (37a4b8e); a `tests-kept` constraint on the review diff (c7e992b); Stop during a busy turn and a single send-back (2b9afae); the add form and each constraint's history (4855dca). 45 core tests, 49 app tests, 2 view tests. Second live exit (2026-10-31) on `j3e0ca30c`, with a charter in `demo-a` (deny `Bash(git push:*)`, a PreToolUse hook that refuses `rm`, a Stop hook that runs pytest): the job page showed the charter, its rule and every hook run; the hook passed 12 calls with exit 0 and refused `rm -f /work/repo/notes.txt` with exit 2 and its own message; the Stop hook ran pytest after each build; with `tests-kept` enforced, a build that dropped `test_add` went back to build with the rule, and at checked the same finding waited for the owner. On the Governance page, the form added `no-curl` (entry 333), History listed `tests-kept`'s promotion and demotion, the chain verified 332 and then 335 entries under the Keychain key, and Export wrote 335 entries and `{\"verified\":true}`. Not run live: the `git push` deny rule (the agent read it in its brief and never made the call; the core and gate tests cover it), and a stalled audit (the unit test covers it). |"," | A6 | done | Spike N9: `judge::evaluate` has no provider worker in this stack, so a run is graded by a harness turn with no tools; `harness::metrics` meters each session (docs/levels.md). Build (38519c5): `Dials::trial` in the core (a trial approves its own plan and stops at review with its diff, so nothing lands), the core's `eval` module (arms, tally from the audit, totals, differences, grade), an arm's rungs applied per trial job in the gate, every turn of every job metered into `turns`, the eval tables, and the Evals page. 51 core tests, 58 app tests. Live exit (2026-10-31), eval `ee8eaaddd` on `demo-a` from `d6227b2`: three requests that each ask for a `wc` count, A with `no-wc` told and B with it enforced. All six runs reached review and were graded. In total B differs from A: refused 0 -> 5, review findings 2 -> 0, turns 39 -> 28, calls 33 -> 17, cost $0.0344 -> $0.0207; grades 7 and 7. Each request lists B's refused calls with their audit entries (#375, #405, #363, #452, ...) and links to the trial job, which shows it stopped at review with Land pending. Apply B set `no-wc` to enforced and the audit recorded `ee8eaaddd arm b: Told -> Enforced` (#487) and the eval the owner acted on (#488). Not varied yet: the model per stage and the pipeline, since there is one of each until A7 and A8. |"," | A7 | done | Built (3605253): the GitHub forge (push `bastion/<job>`, open or reuse the pull request, poll its checks, a bounded CI fix turn with the failing log, merge on Approve), issues as requests that link back and close on merge, versioned settings with Restore, oversight presets, a model per stage from `llm-router`, and the Accounts list; the governance pages split into Constraints, Capabilities and Audit Log with Lucide icons (dbe1cf7). 57 core tests, 66 app tests. Live exit (2026-10-31) on `ianparo/bastion` (private, CI runs pytest and needs a CHANGELOG.md entry): job `j7eb804a7` started from issue #1 and links to it; it opened pull request #2 (`bastion/j7eb804a7`, body `Closes #1`); CI failed on the changelog, Bastion sent the fix turn with the CI log (ci_fixes 1), the fixed change was pushed to the same pull request, and CI passed. Settings: forge set to GitHub (v1), the medium preset set both dials to hold (v2), Restore of v1 wrote v3 with the dials back at ask, and the next job (`ja0b04eb6`) waited at approve with no hold timer. Approve at land then merged pull request #2 into `main` (2beb204) and issue #1 closed. Not run live: a fix turn that fixes CI by itself (see below). |","-| A8 | next | — |","+| A8 | next | First: D26, the harness and factory defaults out of code and into the stack's configuration; the governance pages now show charter, harness and factory sections (D25). |"," | A9 to A13 | — | — |"," | Later (§10) | on hold | — |"," "]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/PLAN.md"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"0484c304-ac0c-4d61-85e1-1f869ccdf6a3","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","root":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","branch":"main","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":6,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":null,"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[],"visibility_cache":[]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"1055538d-2c6b-4cae-a442-e18904bfe5ff","session_id":"135a2369-1f42-433b-aacc-5c1b0ce18b48","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"135a2369-1f42-433b-aacc-5c1b0ce18b48","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"pure-pondering-goose"}
